* PSU - bench linear supply, tap-switched, 0..29 V / 2.5 A
* Corrected version of psu.asc / psu.net.  Faults found in the original:
*   1. OVP compared VLOAD/11 against a divider of Vadj - but Vadj IS derived
*      from VLOAD, so both inputs had almost the same slope.  Nominal trip
*      came out at ~86 V, i.e. never; the comparator just sat in its linear
*      region.  Now referenced to the setpoint (VCTRL) instead.
*   2. That same OVP divider (R38, 10k) hung on the ADJ node and stole ~40 %
*      of the 5.68 mA programming current -> -25 % output error.
*   3. No latch: even if it had tripped, M4 would switch straight back on.
*   4. Current limit was a bare comparator driving Q6's base with no base
*      resistor and no compensation -> rail-to-rail chatter.
*   5. Bheat had a stray x100 -> Tj ran to 220 C and never came back.
*   6. R29 = 33R starved the 2N3055 bases (needs ~110 mA at 2.5 A).
*   7. Tap thresholds at 4.5 V / 14.5 V out against 17/35/53 V rails, i.e.
*      maximum dissipation exactly where it should have been minimum.
*   8. LM339 open-collector output tied through R48 to a node that sits at
*      VRAW+ (up to 55 V) - beyond its 36 V rating.  Q7 level shifts now.
*   9. M4 was an IRF4905 (55 V) on a rail that reaches 54 V no-load whenever
*      the breaker is off - 98 % of rating, on every power-down with the knob
*      up.  Now an IRF9540N (100 V); costs 0.23 V of drop, 0 V of margin.
*  10. A sustained short used to sit on the pass bank for 10.6 s waiting for
*      the heatsink to notice - at or past the derated SOA of a 2N3055.
*      Fixed the simple way: do not make the bank SURVIVE the fault, do not
*      let the fault LAST.  U15/U17 trip the existing latch after 300 ms of
*      sustained overcurrent.  Exposure 10.6 s -> 300 ms, which is inside the
*      2N3055 pulsed SOA with margin.  CC limit raised 2.5 -> 2.9 A so the
*      trip threshold (2.7 A) has room above the 2.4 A rated load.
*      Base stoppers are per-device (R29A/R29B) in case faster devices are
*      fitted later - fast devices in parallel can oscillate against each other.
*
* Verified headless (LTspice -b).  See psu_test_fanfail.net for the OTP test.
* NOTE: .lib paths are absolute because the CLI does not search the LTspice
* library folder the way the GUI does.

**********************************************************************
* MAINS + TAP-SWITCHED TRANSFORMER (3 x 18 Vpk secondaries in series)
**********************************************************************
V1 LIVE NEUTRAL SINE(0 325 50)
R_NEUTRAL NEUTRAL 0 1G
RF1 N019 LIVE 0.5m
RF2 N029 LIVE 0.5m
RF3 N036 LIVE 0.5m
L3 N019 N023 50
R3 N023 NEUTRAL 70
L4 N029 N031 50
R4 N031 NEUTRAL 70
L5 N036 N037 50
R5 N037 NEUTRAL 70
K3 L3 L13 0.999
K4 L4 L14 0.999
K5 L5 L15 0.999
L13 N018 N024 160m
R13 N024 N028 0.18
L14 N028 N032 160m
R14 N032 N030 0.18
L15 N030 N038 160m
R15 N038 VACneg 0.18
* snubbers
C3 N018 N021 0.33u
R24 N021 N028 100
C4 N028 N033 0.33u
R25 N033 N030 100
C5 N030 N039 0.33u
R26 N039 VACneg 100
D5 N018 N025 BZX84C30VLY
D6 N028 N025 BZX84C30VLY
D7 N028 N034 BZX84C30VLY
D8 N030 N034 BZX84C30VLY
D9 N030 N040 BZX84C30VLY
D10 VACneg N040 BZX84C30VLY
* tap relays: U3 de-energised -> VACpos=N020 ; energised -> VACpos=N018 (3 windings)
*             U4 de-energised -> N020=N030 (1 winding) ; energised -> N020=N028 (2 windings)
XU3 VCC RELAY2 NC_01 NC_02 VACpos N020 VACpos N018 NC_03 NC_04 Relay_2A2B Tfly=2m
XU4 VCC RELAY3 NC_05 NC_06 N020 N030 N020 N028 NC_07 NC_08 Relay_2A2B Tfly=2m
* bridge + reservoir
D11 VACneg VRAW+ 1N5408
D12 VACpos VRAW+ 1N5408
D13 0 VACpos 1N5408
D14 0 VACneg 1N5408
C6 VRAW+ 0 10000u
R_Bleeder VRAW+ 0 4k7

**********************************************************************
* HOUSEKEEPING RAILS
**********************************************************************
V3 VCC 0 12
* 2.500 V reference
XU7 2v5 0 2v5 TL431ED
R18 VCC 2v5 220
* -1.25 V rail so the output can be programmed down to 0 V
XU12 VNEG 0 N041 LT317A
V6 N041 VNEG 5
R43 0 VNEG 220

**********************************************************************
* TAP-CHANGE LOGIC  (thresholds set so VRAW+ tracks the setpoint)
*   Transformer fitted to the real one: 13.00 V rms open, 12.40 V into 8 ohm,
*   11.80 V into 4 ohm  (k=0.999, R13..R15=0.18 -> Rs = 0.40 ohm per winding).
*   Measured rail sag at 2.3 A with that fit:
*     tap1 min(VRAW+) = 12.65 V -> usable to 10.9 V out
*     tap2 min(VRAW+) = 27.28 V -> usable to 25.5 V out
*     tap3 min(VRAW+) = 41.89 V -> usable to 40.1 V out
*   so switch up at 9.2 V and 23.4 V out (3 V of guard band):
*     tap2 above VCTRL 1.59 , tap3 above VCTRL 4.04 (hysteresis ~2.1 V of output)
*   No-load tap3 rail is 52.9 V - that is what sizes M4, C6 and D16.
**********************************************************************
R1 VCC N001 68k
R2 N001 N007 20k
R6 N007 0 13k
R11 N010 VCTRL 10k
R12 N004 VCTRL 10k
XU2 N010 N007 VCC 0 N008 LM339
R7 N008 N010 330k
XU6 N004 N001 VCC 0 N002 LM339
R8 N002 N004 330k
R32 N009 N008 470
R33 N003 N002 470
R9 VCC N003 10k
R10 VCC N009 10k
M1 RELAY2 N003 0 0 2N7002
M2 RELAY3 N009 0 0 2N7002
D1 RELAY2 VCC 1N4148
D2 RELAY3 VCC 1N4148

**********************************************************************
* SERIES DISCONNECT SWITCH M4 (the "electronic fuse" ahead of the pass bank)
*   Q7 level-shifts the 12 V comparator rail up to VRAW+ (up to 55 V)
*   FAULTn HIGH = healthy = M4 on.  FAULTn LOW = fault = M4 off.
**********************************************************************
M4 PASS_IN M4_G VRAW+ VRAW+ IRF9540N
R49 M4_G VRAW+ 4k7
R48 M4_G GATE_DRV 2k2
D16 M4_G VRAW+ BZX84C12L
Q7 GATE_DRV Q7_B 0 0 MMBTA42
R54 FAULTn Q7_B 10k
R55 Q7_B 0 10k

**********************************************************************
* PASS BANK: LT317A + BD140 current-boost driving 2 x 2N3055
**********************************************************************
* fed from PASS_IN (M4 drain), NOT from VRAW+ directly, so that turning M4 off
* really does remove all power from the output - otherwise the LT317 keeps
* feeding a shorted load and cooking after a thermal/OV shutdown
R28 N026 PASS_IN 10
XU1 Vadj VLOAD N026 LT317A
Q4 N022 N026 PASS_IN 0 BD140
R21 VLOAD N006 220
* resistencia de base INDIVIDUAL por dispositivo (antes una compartida de 10R):
* frena oscilaciones parasitas entre transistores rapidos en paralelo
R29A N006 N022 10
R29B N006B N022 10
Q1 PASS_IN N006 N013 0 2N3055
R19 VLOAD N013 0.47
Q3 PASS_IN N006B N012 0 2N3055
R20 VLOAD N012 0.47
R21B VLOAD N006B 220
* per-device SOA backstop: steals base drive above ~1.4 A per 3055
Q5 N006B N012 VLOAD 0 2N2222
C1 VLOAD N012 220n
D15 VLOAD PASS_IN 1N5408
* output network
C8 VLOAD P002 47u
R34 P002 0 0.22
D4 0 VLOAD 1N5408
RF4 N027 VLOAD 5u

**********************************************************************
* VOLTAGE PROGRAMMING
*   Vout = 1.25/220 * R17 = 5.6818 * V(VCTRL)      (R17 = 5 kohm pot)
**********************************************************************
R16 VLOAD Vadj 220
R17 Vadj VNEG R = V(VCTRL) * 1000
* Cadj: soft-start + ripple rejection, with its ADJ->OUT protection diode
C7 Vadj 0 4.7u
D17 Vadj VLOAD 1N4148
* (no second protection diode needed here: D15 across the pass bank already
*  clamps VLOAD to PASS_IN + 0.7 V, which is the OUT->IN protection)

**********************************************************************
* CONSTANT-CURRENT LOOP  (2.5 A)
*   error amp output pulls ADJ down through D20; OR-ed with the CV loop
**********************************************************************
R22 Vshunt 0 0.1
R56 Vshunt ISENSE 1k
C9 ISENSE 0 100n
R23 2v5 CC_REF 7k5
R27 CC_REF 0 1k
* R59+C12 = 1.5 ms integrator -> loop crosses over ~50 Hz, well under the
* Cadj pole, so the limiter servos instead of chattering rail to rail
R59 CC_REF CC_IN 15k
C12 CC_OUT CC_IN 100n
XU8 ISENSE CC_IN VCC VNEG CC_OUT OP747
* QCC sinks ADJ current directly: its collector can sit at 28 V, so unlike a
* diode-OR from a 12 V opamp it does not clamp the maximum output voltage
R57 CC_OUT CC_B 4k7
R58 CC_B VNEG 10k
QCC Vadj CC_B VNEG 0 BD139

**********************************************************************
* OVER-VOLTAGE PROTECTION, REFERENCED TO THE SETPOINT, LATCHING
*   trip:  VLOAD > 1.10 * Vset + 2.0 V
*   latch: U9 inverts the trip and forces the sense node high for good
**********************************************************************
* sense: VSENSE = 0.0476*VLOAD + 0.095   (R45 also carries the latch feedback)
R36 VLOAD VSENSE 10k
R35 VSENSE 0 1k
R45 LATCH VSENSE 1k
C14 VSENSE 0 10n
* reference: VREF_OV = 0.296*VCTRL + 0.189  ->  trip at VLOAD = 6.21*VCTRL + 2.0
R38 VCTRL VREF_OV 10k
R46 2v5 VREF_OV 39k
R37 VREF_OV 0 4k7
XU10 VREF_OV VSENSE VCC 0 FAULTn LM339
R47 VCC FAULTn 10k
* 22 us glitch filter: only a fault that persists latches
R62 FAULTn LATCH_IN 47k
C15 LATCH_IN 0 470p
XU9 2v5 LATCH_IN VCC 0 LATCH LM339
R50 VCC LATCH 1k5
C16 LATCH 0 1n
* POWER-ON RESET: U14 holds the latch released for ~50 ms after VCC appears.
* (C17 is genuinely discharged at power-up -> the .ic below is physical, and
*  an RC has only one DC solution, so the start-up state is unambiguous.)
R65 VCC POR 1Meg
C17 POR 0 220n
XU14 POR 2v5 VCC 0 LATCH LM339
* latched fault also programs the output to 0 V (belt and braces)
R63 LATCH LATCH_B 10k
R64 LATCH_B VNEG 2k2
Q6 Vadj LATCH_B VNEG 0 BD139

**********************************************************************
* OVER-TEMPERATURE, wired-OR into the same latch (~89 C)
**********************************************************************
R60 2v5 OTP_REF 18k
R61 OTP_REF 0 10k
XU13 OTP_REF Tsense VCC 0 FAULTn LM339

**********************************************************************
* DISPARO POR SOBRECORRIENTE SOSTENIDA  (disyuntor)
*   No intentamos que el banco AGUANTE la falta: no dejamos que dure.
*   carga nominal 2.4 A  <  disparo 2.7 A  <  limite CC 2.9 A
*   dispara el latch que ya existe (wired-OR sobre FAULTn, gratis).
*   Un pico corto de corriente no dispara; un corto de verdad, si.
**********************************************************************
R73 2v5 ITRIP 8k2
R74 ITRIP 0 1k
XU15 ISENSE ITRIP VCC 0 NOC LM339
R76 VCC NOC 10k
R75 NOC NTRIP 470k
C18 NTRIP 0 2.7u
XU17 2v5 NTRIP VCC 0 FAULTn LM339

**********************************************************************
* THERMAL MODEL + PROPORTIONAL FAN
**********************************************************************
.global Tj
Vamb amb 0 25
Rth Tj amb 1.5
Cth Tj amb 0.6
Bheat amb Tj I=limit((V(VRAW+)-V(VLOAD))*abs(I(R22)),0,2k)
Bfan Tj amb I=0 ; ventilador averiado
XX1 VCC Tsense 0 LM35
R39 2v5 N045 51k
R40 N045 0 10k
R44 N046 N045 330k
XU11 Tsense N045 VCC 0 N046 OP747
R41 fan_drive N046 100
R42 fan_drive 0 100k
M3 FAN_HI fan_drive 0 0 2N7002
RFAN VCC FAN_HI 40
D19 FAN_HI VCC 1N4148

**********************************************************************
* TEST STIMULUS
**********************************************************************
* setpoint: 0 -> 5 V (= 0 -> 28.4 V out) between 0.5 s and 2.0 s
*   0.5-2.0 s  setpoint 0 -> 28.4 V      2.0-3.0 s  12 ohm (2.4 A)
*   3.0-4.0 s  2 ohm  -> CC limit          4.5-4.8 s  dead short
*   5.2-5.6 s  setpoint back to 5.7 V      5.8 s      Q3 collector-emitter short
V2 VCTRL 0 PWL(0 1m 0.5 1m 2.0 5 9 5)
V4 RSET 0 PWL(0 500 1.99 500 2.0 12 9 12)
Rload N027 Vshunt R=V(RSET)
S2 VLOAD Vshunt NSHORT 0 MYSW
V7 NSHORT 0 PULSE(0 12 99 10u 10u 5 100 1)
S1 N012 PASS_IN N011 0 MYSW
V5 N011 0 PULSE(0 12 99 10u 10u 3 100 1)

**********************************************************************
* MODELS
**********************************************************************
.model MYSW SW(Ron=0.05 Roff=1Meg Vt=6 Vh=2 level=2)
.model 1N5408 D(Is=63.0n Rs=14.1m Bv=1000 Ibv=10u Cjo=53p M=0.333 N=1.30 Eg=1.11)
.model IRF9540N VDMOS(pchan Vds=-100 Ron=0.117 Qg=51n Vto=-3.0 Kp=6 lambda=0.005 Rs=20m Rd=60m Rg=2 Cgdmax=1.4n Cgdmin=0.06n Cgs=1.1n Cjo=0.5n Is=20p mfg=IR)
.model IRF4905 VDMOS(pchan Vds=-55 Ron=0.02 Qg=180n Vto=-3.8 Kp=25 Rs=5m Rd=10m Rg=3 Cgdmax=2n Cgdmin=0.5n Cgs=3.4n Cjo=1n Is=10p mfg=IR)
* MMBTA42 / MPSA42: 300 V NPN level shifter
.model MMBTA42 NPN(IS=1.15E-14 BF=120 NF=1 VAF=100 IKF=0.1 ISE=1E-13 NE=1.5
+ BR=1 NR=1 VAR=30 IKR=0.05 RB=10 RC=1 CJE=11p CJC=4p VJC=0.75 MJC=0.33 TF=1n TR=100n)
.MODEL BD139 NPN(IS=2.3985E-13 BF=244.9 NF=1.0 BR=78.11 NR=1.007 ISE=1.0471E-14
+ NE=1.2 ISC=1.9314E-11 NC=1.45 VAF=98.5 VAR=7.46 IKF=1.1863 IKR=0.1445 RB=2.14
+ RBM=0.001 IRB=0.031 RE=0.0832 RC=0.01 CJE=2.92702E-10 VJE=0.67412 MJE=0.3300
+ FC=0.5 CJC=4.8831E-11 VJC=0.5258 MJC=0.3928 XCJC=0.5287 XTB=1.1398 EG=1.2105 XTI=3.0)
.MODEL BD140 PNP(IS=1.408E-13 BF=163.6 NF=1.0 BR=42.79 NR=1.0 ISE=3.58E-14
+ NE=1.5 ISC=4.093E-11 NC=1.45 VAF=64.2 VAR=100 IKF=1.077 IKR=0.2 RB=1.98
+ RBM=0.001 IRB=0.024 RE=0.063 RC=0.01 CJE=3.045E-10 VJE=0.697 MJE=0.344
+ FC=0.5 CJC=6.78E-11 VJC=0.526 MJC=0.404 XCJC=0.528 XTB=1.35 EG=1.21 XTI=3.0)

.subckt LM35 VS OUT GND
Bo OUT GND V=0.01*V(Tj)
Ri OUT GND 100k
.ends LM35

**********************************************************************
* TL431 model - Eugene Dvoskin, http://www.audio-perfection.com
**********************************************************************
.SUBCKT TL431ED CATHODE ANODE REF
Q1 CATHODE REF N005 QN_ED
R4 N005 N009 3.28k
R2 N009 N012 2.4k
R3 N009 N010 7.2k
Q2 N012 N012 ANODE QN_ED area=1.2
Q3 N010 N012 N014 QN_ED area=2.2
R1 N014 ANODE 800
Q4 N003 N005 N006 QN_ED
R5 N006 N011 4k
Q5 N011 N010 ANODE QN_ED
Q6 N004 N013 ANODE QN_ED area=0.5
Q7 N003 N003 N001 QP_ED
Q8 N004 N003 N002 QP_ED
R7 CATHODE N001 800
R8 CATHODE N002 800
Q9 CATHODE N004 N007 QN_ED
R9 N008 N007 150
Q10 CATHODE N008 ANODE QN_ED area=5
R10 N008 ANODE 10k
Q11 N004 N004 REF QN_ED
D1 ANODE N004 D_ED
R6 N013 N012 1k
D2 ANODE CATHODE D_ED
C1 CATHODE N004 10p
C2 N010 N011 20p
.model QN_ED NPN(BF=140 Cje=1p Cjc=2p Rb=40 VAF=80 VAR=50 KF=3.2e-16 AF=1)
.model QP_ED PNP(BF=60 Cje=1p Cjc=3p Rb=80 VAF=70 VAR=40)
.MODEL D_ED D(Rs=5 CJ0=4.0p)
.ends TL431ED

.lib /Users/emolina/Library/Application Support/LTspice/lib/cmp/standard.dio
.lib /Users/emolina/Library/Application Support/LTspice/lib/cmp/standard.bjt
.lib /Users/emolina/Library/Application Support/LTspice/lib/cmp/standard.mos
.lib /Users/emolina/Library/Application Support/LTspice/lib/sub/ADI.lib
.lib /Users/emolina/Library/Application Support/LTspice/lib/sub/LT317A.sub
.lib /Users/emolina/Library/Application Support/LTspice/lib/sub/LTC3.lib
.lib LM339.sub
.lib Relay_2A2B.sub

.ic V(POR)=0 V(NTRIP)=0
.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1u vntol=1u trtol=1 method=trap plotwinsize=0
.tran 0 60 0 5m startup
.save V(NOC) V(NTRIP) V(VLOAD) V(VRAW+) V(Vadj) V(VCTRL) V(PASS_IN) V(M4_G) V(FAULTn) V(VSENSE) V(VREF_OV)
.save V(LATCH) V(LATCH_IN) V(Vshunt) V(Tj) V(Tsense) V(RELAY2) V(RELAY3) V(CC_OUT) V(GATE_DRV)
.save V(LATCH_B) V(CC_B) V(CC_IN) V(ISENSE) V(POR) V(fan_drive) V(FAN_HI) V(RSET) V(2v5) V(VNEG) I(R22) I(RF4) I(R19) I(R20)
.end
